  "request": {
    "spec": "Consolidate all duplicate detection into a single derived 'identityKey' = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId, and reject with 409 only when a new owner's WHOLE identityKey equals an existing owner's. This changes existing behaviour: the separate telephone, email and household duplicate checks must now be expressed through this one key. Because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same householdId) with different telephones have different identityKeys and must both be allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. Return 'identityKey'.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies the\nspecification and all existing and new tests pass.\n\nWrite it to keep structural impact low. Structural impact is a measurable cost, not a\nvague goal. For every function you change, the cost is:\n    cost = max(WMC_other, 1) * CC * max(1, changed_lines)\nCC is that function's cyclomatic complexity. WMC_other is the summed cyclomatic\ncomplexity of the OTHER methods in its class, which is the surrounding context you must\nhold to edit it safely. changed_lines is how many of its lines you add or edit. The costs\nare summed over every function you change, then multiplied by the number of files you\ntouch. So the biggest lever is WMC_other: a method inside a large class pays for the whole\nclass. Do not grow one method or one class. Add behaviour as small, cohesive units, each\nwith little surrounding complexity, and keep every function you change simple.\n\nRun the test suite and make it green before finishing.\n\nConsolidate all duplicate detection into a single derived 'identityKey' = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId, and reject with 409 only when a new owner's WHOLE identityKey equals an existing owner's. This changes existing behaviour: the separate telephone, email and household duplicate checks must now be expressed through this one key. Because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same householdId) with different telephones have different identityKeys and must both be allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. Return 'identityKey'.\n"
  },
